{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T23:01:12+00:00", "step": "omissions-20261127T225710Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-04i", "kind": "omission", "seed": 57416617415334, "ruling_id": "9e8112341516835d", "prompt_sha256": "bcae380e4e2b9bf580f406b62337b15840bfbeaad845f8b9da48634b5e10d6d0", "inputs_sha256": "3c05787511b628894f424ea641a64986a181cc780ca6f3416102fa5749151052", "first": {"ruling": "add", "text": "The IPCC assessment finds, with high confidence, that transitioning towards net zero CO2 emissions faster and reducing non-CO2 emissions such as methane more rapidly would limit peak warming levels and reduce the requirement for net negative CO2 emissions, thereby reducing feasibility and sustainability concerns, and social and environmental risks associated with CDR deployment at large scales [1]."}, "second": {"ruling": "add", "text": "The IPCC assessment finds, with high confidence, that transitioning towards net zero CO2 emissions faster and reducing non-CO2 emissions such as methane more rapidly would limit peak warming levels and reduce the requirement for net negative CO2 emissions, thereby reducing feasibility and sustainability concerns, and social and environmental risks associated with CDR deployment at large scales [1]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": true, "usage": {"input": 5995, "output": 832, "usd": 0.04062, "seconds": 7.1}, "applied": false}
{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T23:01:19+00:00", "step": "omissions-20261127T225710Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-04i", "kind": "omission", "seed": 57416617415334, "ruling_id": "42854938000fe75e", "prompt_sha256": "bcae380e4e2b9bf580f406b62337b15840bfbeaad845f8b9da48634b5e10d6d0", "inputs_sha256": "4fdccba82813b34adb862eac3ca57c1f6bb2941e0ef7624b97b39be839d66b97", "first": {"ruling": "add", "text": "The IPCC chapter states plainly that, within ambitious mitigation strategies at global or national levels, CDR cannot serve as a substitute for deep emissions reductions but can fulfil multiple complementary roles [2]."}, "second": {"ruling": "add", "text": "The IPCC chapter states plainly that, within ambitious mitigation strategies at global or national levels, CDR cannot serve as a substitute for deep emissions reductions but can fulfil multiple complementary roles [2]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": true, "usage": {"input": 3799, "output": 711, "usd": 0.029416, "seconds": 7.1}, "applied": false}
{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T23:01:25+00:00", "step": "omissions-20261127T225710Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-04i", "kind": "omission", "seed": 57416617415334, "ruling_id": "5ef359709cbfbf86", "prompt_sha256": "bcae380e4e2b9bf580f406b62337b15840bfbeaad845f8b9da48634b5e10d6d0", "inputs_sha256": "cda2e1e73c6b2774e07eddf0b72e6b1051a837320b17e9709a500eaaca0ccbbf", "first": {"ruling": "add", "text": "The IPCC chapter qualifies this sequence, noting that 'in general, these roles of CDR are not mutually exclusive and can exist in parallel' [2]."}, "second": {"ruling": "add", "text": "The IPCC chapter qualifies this sequence, noting that \"in general, these roles of CDR are not mutually exclusive and can exist in parallel\" [2]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": false, "usage": {"input": 3616, "output": 568, "usd": 0.025824, "seconds": 5.5}, "applied": false}
